      "details": "<p>Writing for <em>Brill's New Pauly</em>, Giovanni Uggeri indicates that the <em>Simbruinus ager</em> was considered a part of the territory of the Aequi. This <em>ager</em> was located at the foot of the <em>colles Simbruini</em>, as attested in Tacitus.</p>",
